title: Prove typed-draft preservation in real tmux Codex sessions
---
Depends on the remote launcher and passive ingress adapter.

Build a real-tmux E2E harness using existing scripts. It must deliberately leave non-empty text in the Codex composer, send inbound c2c mail, and inspect behavior before and after submit.

Acceptance criteria:
- The exact composer text and cursor position are unchanged when a message arrives.
- No turn is started, cancelled, or steered merely by message arrival.
- The passive message becomes available to Codex at a validated lifecycle point, and multi-message ordering/dedupe is checked.
- Cover idle, actively-generating, disconnected app-server, and ordinary non-remote Codex fallback.
- Capture reproducible tmux receipts and run the tests inside the slice worktree.

Blockers: P1.M1.E1.T002 and P1.M1.E1.T003.